  "as_of": "2020-03-23",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would add funding for ordinary Commonwealth services delivering the coronavirus response, including health care, employment support, aviation assistance and payment administration.",
   "It would allocate money through departmental, administered and corporate entity appropriations, with an additional ministerial advance of up to $800 million for urgent shortfalls.",
   "It would commence on royal assent and accompany a separate appropriation bill for services outside ordinary annual government operations in the coronavirus package."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "Respiratory clinics for diagnosing and managing coronavirus and other respiratory illnesses would receive $113.5 million.",
   "The bill would allocate $250.0 million towards waiving Airservices Australia charges for domestic airlines.",
   "Services Australia would receive $221.0 million for stimulus payments and additional Medicare processing linked to coronavirus pathology testing."
  ],
  "affected": "Commonwealth agencies, health and aged care providers, airlines and employers would be affected.",
